# The root .gitattributes normalizes everything to LF. That is wrong for two
# files here, and both failures are silent:
#
#   *.bat  - a batch file is consumed by cmd.exe on Windows. Store LF, check out
#            CRLF, so what ships is what Windows expects.
#   *.ps1  - keep LF, but never let git "fix" the file: the UTF-8 BOM at the top
#            is load-bearing. Without it Windows PowerShell 5.1 reads the script
#            as ANSI and every Hebrew string in the UI turns to garbage.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=lf
